Bluetooth: L2CAP: add the missing l2cap_chan_hold_unless_zero()

l2cap_core.c calls l2cap_chan_hold_unless_zero() when it looks a channel
up by command identifier, but the function does not exist anywhere in this
tree, and with CONFIG_BT=y clang refuses the implicit declaration:

  net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c:3989:9: error: implicit declaration of
  function 'l2cap_chan_hold_unless_zero'

The tree already keeps an atomic kref per channel, so implement it with
kref_get_unless_zero(), which returns 0 when the last reference is gone.
The call site already treats NULL as "no such channel".
--- a/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c	2026-11-14 13:47:50
+++ b/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c	2026-11-14 13:47:50
@@ -484,6 +484,16 @@
 	BT_DBG("chan %p orig refcnt %d", c, atomic_read(&c->kref.refcount));
 
 	kref_get(&c->kref);
+}
+
+static struct l2cap_chan *l2cap_chan_hold_unless_zero(struct l2cap_chan *c)
+{
+	BT_DBG("chan %p orig refcnt %d", c, atomic_read(&c->kref.refcount));
+
+	if (!kref_get_unless_zero(&c->kref))
+		return NULL;
+
+	return c;
 }
 
 void l2cap_chan_put(struct l2cap_chan *c)
